<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine tax chief seeks more power to shut firms.</title>
<headline>Argentine tax chief seeks more power to shut firms.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's newly-appointed taxation chief Carlos Silvani said he will seek added powers from Congress to shut businesses that fail to pay their taxes.</p>
<p>Silvani wants the DGI tax office to be allowed to close firms without having to involve the Commerce Secretariat, which usually involves substantial delays, he told reporters late Wednesday.</p>
<p>Silvani, who took over the tax office Tuesday, said he believes the power to close shops is a most effective deterrent to tax evasion.</p>
<p>-- Daniel Helft, Buenos Aires Newsroom + 541 318 0663</p>
</text>
